@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title proveo-entrypoint prep — what does and does NOT cross the process boundary

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {

  component "defs/<name>/entrypoint.sh\n(PID 1 shell — execs the agent)" as SH <<app>>

  component "proveo-entrypoint prep <target>\n(child process)" as PREP <<app>>

  frame "Crosses the boundary\n(external to the process)" as OK {
    component "ensure_runtime_user\npasswd entry + writable HOME" as UID <<app>>
    component "report_git_context\nstdout preamble" as GITCTX <<app>>
    component "attach_rtk\nfilesystem" as RTK <<app>>
    component "SmokeReady\nprints sentinel, sleeps" as SMOKE <<async>>
  }

  frame "Dies with the child\n(process-local state)" as LOST <<error>> {
    component "set_working_directory\nchdir(2)" as CWD <<error>>
    component "load_env\nsource .env → exports" as ENV <<error>>
    component "ApplyEnvBridges\nOPENCODE_MODEL, …" as BRIDGE <<error>>
    component "bridge_git_identity\nGIT_CONFIG_KEY_n exports" as GITID <<error>>
  }

  component "agent CLI\n(inherits the SHELL's env + cwd)" as AGENT <<app>>
}

SH ARROW_MAIN PREP : " ""proveo-entrypoint prep <target> || true"" "
PREP ARROW_MAIN OK : effects outlive the child
PREP ARROW_ERROR LOST : errorLabel(discarded on exit)
SH ARROW_MAIN AGENT : " ""exec <agent> \"$@\""" "

note right of LOST
  **A child cannot mutate its parent.**
  ""chdir"" and ""setenv"" are per-process. ""prep"" exits 0
  whether or not any of this took effect, so the failure
  is **silent** — the agent simply starts with the image
  ""WORKDIR"" and no project env.

  Observed before this was specified:
  * opencode ignored ""ARCHITECT_MODEL"" → baked default
  * claudecode had no ""ANTHROPIC_MODEL"" at all
  * ""find_env_file"" searched the wrong directory
    (masked in real runs only because ""proveo run""
     passes ""docker run -w /app"")
end note

note bottom of SH
  **Contract for def entrypoints.** After calling ""prep"",
  redo the process-local steps IN THIS SHELL:
  ""set_working_directory <dir>"" then ""load_env quiet""
  then the harness's own model bridge. All are idempotent
  and only fill slots still unset, so a value already
  supplied by ""docker run -e"" wins.

  ""load_env"" must never delegate back to ""prep"" — a
  function whose job is exporting cannot do it from a
  subprocess. See _spec/packages/lib/steps.puml.
end note

note top of SMOKE
  **Still owned by prep:** under ""PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST=1""
  ""prep"" prints ""PROVEO_SMOKE_READY"" and sleeps, so
  anything a def prints *after* ""prep"" is unreachable in
  smoke mode. Defs whose tests assert their own preamble
  must run ""prep"" with the flag cleared and call
  ""run_smoke_test"" at the end of their own preamble.
end note
note bottom of PREP
  **The prelude is one Go binary shared by every entrypoint**: runtime user,
  ""\.env"" load, env bridges, git identity, smoke mode, credential
  sentinel. A harness entrypoint that reimplemented any of these would
  drift from the others, and this is the layer whose failures are hardest
  to see from inside a container.

  **What it forwards by value is deliberately only the non-secret half** —
  the model and UI preferences from the shared baseline plus the harness's
  own ""config:"" list. They cannot carry a credential by construction:
  secrets are declared in ""env:"" and travel through the broker instead.
end note


@enduml
